<main class="wrap1 txt legal-page"><nav class="crumb"><a href="./">Home</a> / Refunds and Returns</nav><h1 class="ph1">Refunds, Returns and Cancellations</h1><p class="fine">Last updated: 24 November 2026</p>
<p>We want your order to arrive as expected. This policy explains how to contact us about an order. It does not remove or limit any rights you have under consumer law.</p>
<h2>Something is wrong with an item</h2><p>If an item is missing, incorrect, damaged, not as described, or faulty, contact us as soon as you can on <a href="https://wa.me/<?=e(wa_number())?>">WhatsApp <?=e(wa_display())?></a>. Include your order reference, the item and what happened. For damaged or incorrect goods, a photo can help us understand the issue. We will review it with you and explain the available remedy.</p>
<p>Consumer law provides remedies when goods are faulty, not as described, or do not meet the required standard. Depending on the circumstances, this can include a refund, repair or replacement. The short-term right to reject faulty goods is generally available within 30 days of receiving them. Your legal rights apply whether an item was full price or on sale.</p>
<h2>Changing your mind about an online order</h2><p>For eligible goods bought at a distance, you may have a legal right to cancel within 14 days after the day you receive the goods, without giving a reason. Tell us clearly that you wish to cancel by contacting us on WhatsApp or using the optional template below. This right does not apply to every product: for example, the law excludes goods liable to deteriorate or expire rapidly, and certain sealed hygiene goods once unsealed. The exact exception depends on the goods.</p>
<p>If you are unsure whether an item can be cancelled or returned, contact us before sending or bringing it back. Please keep goods safe and do not return perishable or temperature-sensitive items without agreeing safe handling with us first. This does not affect your rights if goods are faulty or not as described.</p>
<h2>Orders not yet collected or delivered</h2><p>If you need to cancel or change an order before collection or delivery, message us as soon as possible with your order reference. We will confirm whether preparation has started and what options are available. A cancellation request made before we accept an order can be withdrawn without charge.</p>
<h2>How refunds are handled</h2><p>Once we agree that a refund is due, we will confirm the amount and arrange it in line with applicable legal time limits. For bank transfers, we may need your payment details to return the funds; never send a full card number or security code. Where payment was made on collection or delivery, we will agree a suitable way to make the refund.</p>
<h2>Optional cancellation message</h2><p>You can send a clear message instead of using this template. If helpful, copy and complete:</p><div class="policy-template"><p>To: Skye African Supermarket, <?=e(shop_address())?></p><p>I am giving notice that I wish to cancel my distance-sale order.</p><p>Order reference:</p><p>Item(s) to cancel:</p><p>Name:</p><p>Address:</p><p>Date the order was placed / goods received:</p><p>Date of this message:</p></div>
<h2>Contact us</h2><p>WhatsApp: <a href="https://wa.me/<?=e(wa_number())?>"><?=e(wa_display())?></a><br>Store: <?=e(shop_address())?></p><p>See also our <a href="delivery">Delivery and Collection</a> information and <a href="terms">Terms and Conditions</a>.</p>
